  m_Name: Blade12
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade12
  description: The Blade12 is a tiny, thin-flat blade situated at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, constructed from Blades2 material, responsible for compressing
    and accelerating the air flowing through the engine, with an interesting aspect
    being its carefully designed shape for maximizing airflow efficiency. Its small
    size and thin-flat shape allow it to operate effectively at high speeds, making
    it a critical component of the engine's compressor stage. By working in tandem
    with other blades, Blade12 helps to achieve the high compression ratios necessary
    for efficient engine operation, thereby contributing to the engine's overall
    performance.
